# Act of Treason "can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control" (its ruling). Bot1 casts
# Llanowar Elves and then Act of Treason on it: Bot1 gains control of what it already controls (CR 613.1b), and the Elves
# gains haste, so though it came under Bot1's control this turn it attacks Bot2 for 1 (CR 302.6, 702.10). When the effect
# ends with the turn, its controller is the one it had before any control effect: Bot1 still (CR 613.1b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Act of Treason
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.SummoningSick = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Act of Treason.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = Haste
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Emerald; Forest; Mountain; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Life = 19
